# .env is committed on purpose - it holds non-secret defaults (the
# container start mode and the relative API base URL) that every checkout
# needs, and docker-compose.yml names it in env_file, so a clone without
# it cannot start at all. Machine-specific overrides and anything secret
# belong in .env.local, which the *.local rule above already ignores.
